	"data": "Stanford University — CS Graduate Programs (HCI/XR Focus)\n\nPart of [[projects/grad-school-options|Grad School Options]] research.\n\nOverview\n\nStanford University is one of the birthplaces of modern VR/AR research. The Virtual Human Interaction Lab (VHIL), founded in 2003 by Jeremy Bailenson, has been a global leader in studying how virtual experiences transform education, empathy, environmental conservation, and health. Stanford's Computer Science department offers both PhD and MS programs, with…",
